<!--Post: 3384--><!--Time: 1104857026-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3384"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Devbost<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Devbost<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 8:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think the drug angle is a dead end. There has been nothing whatsoever &#40;that I&#39;ve seen, anyway&#41; to suggest that there is any drug connection to the Otero family. <BR> <BR>As for the Bright murder/shooting, the Brights were in their late teens/early 20s, and it was the 70s. There may have been drugs present, but there&#39;s nothing connecting that to their being attacked. <BR> <BR>The Wegerles were obviously churchgoing people, and had small children and were known to the community and their neighbors. Zero drug connection there. <BR> <BR>BTK kills to serve other needs. It has nothing to do with drugs.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3384-->
<!--Post: 3442--><!--Time: 1104897482-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3442"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 7:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Devbost et al: <BR> <BR>This is not about linking the Oteros to drugs.  <BR> <BR> The Point Is: Why Was Mr. Otero AFRAID For Days &#42;BEFORE&#42; repeat &#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;BEFORE&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42; he was killed? <BR> <BR>on 12/1/2004, Charlie Otero told an AP reporter in a phone interview that he thought his father knew BTK, that when power went out in the house his father made the family get into a closet until he was sure that power was out in the other houses.  A few days before his death, his father tried to give Charlie his ring &#34;in case something happened to him&#34;  Here is a link to the interview: <a href="http://dodgeglobe.com/stories/120104/state_120104008.shtml" target=_top>http://dodgeglobe.com/stories/120104/state_1201040 08.shtml</a>  <BR> <BR>This isn&#39;t about drugs, it&#39;s about that statement. <BR> <BR>If Mr. Otero knew about this threat before: <BR> <BR>1.  How did he know? <BR> <BR>2.  Why didn&#39;t he ask the police for help? <BR> <BR>3.  Why did someone want to harm him/his family? <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3442-->
<!--Post: 3472--><!--Time: 1104949113-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3472"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Devbost<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Devbost<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 10:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Whoisbtk: <BR> <BR>I agree with you that Mr. Otero&#39;s behavior is a pertinent avenue of exploration. However, let me play Devil&#39;s Advocate. <BR> <BR>Let&#39;s forget for just a moment that the Oteros became murder victims. Is it possible that Mr. Otero&#39;s strange behavior was due to simple paranoia? It has been suggested that Mr. Otero&#39;s past professional history may have gotten him into a situation that ultimately led to the deaths of him and his family. But isn&#39;t it also a possibility that the work he did put him into the habit of watching his back and worrying for his safety, perhaps so much so that it became something of an obsession? So much so that the entire family learned Judo? So much so that a power outage could drive him to hide the family in a closet? <BR> <BR>How do we know that the threat that Mr. Otero feared was a real one? Why exactly does Charlie Otero think that his father knew BTK? <BR> <BR>The timing of Mr. Otero giving Charlie his ring is indeed cause for raising a red flag. But I also think that a plausible case could be made that the two events are coincidental to each other. There is nothing to suggest that the two events are related in any way aside from the timing. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m not saying that you are wrong in the suppositions you&#39;re making, or that anyone trying to piece together theories about possible connections between BTK and the Oteros is going down a dead-end street. <BR> <BR>What I <b>am</b> saying is that most of the discussion here about the Oteros seems to be framed around the assumption that Mr. Otero&#39;s odd behavior is evidence of some pre-existing link between the family and the killer. What I am doing is challenging that assumption. <BR> <BR>Let&#39;s say that the threat was absolutely real, and that Mr. Otero&#39;s history did indeed catch up with him on the day he and his family were murdered. If BTK was simply exacting revenge on Mr. Otero for some past wrong, then how does one explain the ritualism of the murders, when a bullet to the head would have sufficed? How does one explain the semen that was found scattered around the house? <BR> <BR>If you&#39;re worried that you&#39;re going to be a victim of a professional hit by drug dealers or the government, then it&#39;s plausible that you might think that the police will be no help to you, because the people you&#39;re worried about are beyond the reach of the police. <BR> <BR>On the other hand, why would anyone have reason to believe they might be the victim of a serial killer until it actually happens to them? If Mr. Otero was worried about this sort of thing, it does appear counterintuitive for him to not have sought the help of the police, since they obviously would be able to help him in that kind of situation. <BR> <BR>Someone suggested that BTK was there to do something of a professional hit on the family, and discovered his serial killer tendencies in the act. Unless that theory is dead-on correct, then the pieces here don&#39;t fit. I have no idea what the missing parts are, but there are gaps in the narrative here that make any theories problematic in the absence of more information than the WPD is willing to give.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3472-->
<!--Post: 3480--><!--Time: 1104955749-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3480"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 12:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Is it plausible that Mr. O&#39;s behaviour is related to the shooting of Michael Williams?  And by extension, perhaps also to people or things going on at Coleman? <BR> <BR>The M.W. shooting, even though intriguing, just doesn&#39;t have a BTK ring to it for me.  However, it still could explain Mr. O.&#39;s extreme nervousness. <BR> <BR>But, to go in a completely different direction, these statements of Charlie&#39;s are awfully intriguing to me, yet I don&#39;t think they&#39;ve been persued: <BR> <BR>&#34;... &#39;I am sure it had something to do with my father&#39;s military history. My dad did things. ... He had to tell somebody what he had been up to in the last few years and he was dead days later.&#39; <BR> <BR>[Then Charlie described that his father trained Latin American Air Force personell] <BR> <BR>But Otero declined to say further what his father did in the military because he was afraid talking about it might jeopardize his parole next month.&#34; <BR> <BR>Odd. <BR> <BR>Also, this may point back to the drug plane crash.  Rather than being &#42;involved&#42; in the drug ring, which to all accounts seems unlikely, perhaps he had trained, worked with, or otherwise knew the people trafiking the drugs.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3480-->
<!--Post: 3495--><!--Time: 1104965732-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3495"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 2:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Question: Is there any [B]other[B] references to BTK having a [B]dark complexion[B] than the eyewitness testimony of the neighbor of the Otero&#39;s? <BR> <BR>The Otero parents had a dark complexion and eyewitness testimony is very unreliable. <BR> <BR>If I&#39;m not mistaken, all the other accounts, post office @ 4:00am, Bill Bright, the Vian Children... etc. don&#39;t say he is anything but a &#34;white&#34; male... do they?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3495-->
<!--Post: 3520--><!--Time: 1104974420-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3520"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bargle<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bargle<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 5:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;s also possible that what Mr. Otero was afraid of and BTK are completely unrelated. Just because he had reason to be worried, it does not automaticly follow that what he was afraid of was BTK. <BR>A crude analogy: someone being very careful about crossing the street only to be struck by lightning.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3520-->
<!--Post: 3528--><!--Time: 1104977377-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3528"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 6:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The murderer of the Otero&#39;s was a parafile who&#39;s paraphelia was at first fantasy followed by masturbation and then fantasy turned to action. This sexual devient instilled fear through force and asserted control by maintaining control over the victims through con&#39;s, ruse and physical restraint.  <BR>This guy wasn&#39;t on drugs before or during his crimes but may have been soon after to escalate his reliving to the murders. <BR>Asphixia through strangulation or suffocation was not only his prefered way of dispatching his victims it also was his sexual thrill highlighted by bondage and using objects for touching, probing and tampering with his victims bodies while alive and after they died. <BR>He knew who was there and who wasn&#39;t. He planned well and took with him all that he would need. He had plenty of rope for binding his victims. So much in fact that he had enough to spare for the other two children had they been home. He used exessive binding on the daugther as he bound her well and hung her from a pipe. <BR>He allowed himself plenty of pre-planned time he would spend at the Otero&#39;s to fully enjoy his killing spree and sexual release.  <BR>This wasn&#39;t his first time. It may have been his first major success. He may have killed or tried to kill before but something went wrong and he learned from his mistakes. This time there would be no mistakes and no witnesses. <BR>After his repeated exhillerations his confidence waned but his getaway was so smooth and effortless he suprised even himself.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3528-->
<!--Post: 3637--><!--Time: 1105077152-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3637"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 9:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;One possibility is that the fallout from telling police was as bad or worse than dealing with the threat privately. If he goes to the police and says someone is trying to kill me they’ll ask me Who and Why.&#34; <BR> <BR>Mike, how about the possibility of some top secret military situation in which Mr. Otero felt the goverment wanted to protect the secret, whatever it was, over his family? I am just thinking out loud here but, given this possible scenario, it would cut the same way as the criminal conspiracy angle, wouldn&#39;t it? Perhaps BTK and Mr. Otero were billeted to the same top secret assignment and something happened during that mission that Mr. Otero COULD NOT talk about to civilian authorities. Perhaps BTK committed a serious war crime while on a mission, or simply a murder while in such a place or situation that the government could not acknowlege it without serious repercussions.  <BR>SOMETHING along these lines might be a possible alternative to BTK and Mr. Otero being involved together in a criminal conspiracy. Perhaps they were involved in a top secret military conspiracy, or something similar. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3637-->
<!--Post: 3639--><!--Time: 1105077730-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3639"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 10:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is starting to sound somewhat like Lethal Weapon....maybe a covert CIA thing involving Joseph Otero and of course BTK..or possibly an anticommunist thing built around the Latin American airforce training Otero did...Someone might want to see if there is a file on the father Otero..use the Freedom of Information Act and see if there&#39;s any files that mention his name that are classified...If there are that could provoke some comment...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
