<!--Post: 3643--><!--Time: 1105078590-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3643"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 10:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I am convinced that BTK knew Joseph Otero and possibly, most likely probably, all of the other victims as well.  <BR>Have WPD or the FBI ever actually examined commonalities between all 8 of the known &#40;there are almost certainly unknown&#41; victims and excluded a common connection positively? Did any of the victims know each other? Was there something they had in common; job, Church, school, bridge club, masonic lodge, Shockers sports fans, anything? I think the issue of any of the victims knowing any of the other victims is particularly important to ascertain. <BR>I also find the Coleman production line connection interesting although Chief Hannon rejected it as significant early in the investigation - after the suceeding murders that should have been closely reexamined. I feel that the key, however, is to be found at least in part in Mr. Otero&#39;s military service. There HAS to be some kind of connection somewhere there. The BTK murders were way too passionate and well planned to be simply random murders of strangers, particularly in the case of the Oteros.  <BR>Based on what Charlie Otero has said about his father&#39;s behavior in the days prior to the murders, there is a clear probability that Mr. Otero was fearful of something or someone, of some clear and present danger to his family that was imminently present. Is it possible that BTK committed a crime that was witnessed by Mr. Otero? Perhaps it is more plausible that Mr. Otero saw or heard or knew something about BTK that was connected through the military that he was pretty sure someone would kill to keep secret? Charlie Otero has said on several occasions that he belives his father knew BTK and also knew that a threat to his family was real and immediate &#40;checking for the lights being out elsewhere during a power failure before letting the kids out of a closet, having Charlie look out the window for a service truck before opening the door to a serviceman, giving Charlie his ring for &#34;safekeeping&#34;, etc.&#41; Clearly Mr. Otero had SOME reason to be deeply concerned. <BR>Charlie also said something in one particular interview that has flown pretty much under the radar but which I find truly remarkable - he said that he was told that his father, during the course of the Otero homicides, was UNbound and forced to write something down before being REbound and killed &#40;does anyone remember exactly where Charlie said this? I could not locate it&#41;. IF it is accurate it is very disturbing since it indicates that BTK both knew Mr. Otero and also had some kind of connection with him that was a secret worth killing an entire family over &#40;another possibility is that perhaps BTK forced Mr. Otero, by threatening his children and wife, to sign over something of value or importance, or perhaps there was a military secret involved&#41;. Granted, Charlie Otero has not always been 100% consistent in his statements, so this is possibly not accurate. Does anyone KNOW if it is one way or the other?  <BR>I believe it is silly to think that BTK did NOT know his victims SOMEHOW. Discovering what that common connection is seems to me to be something that would shed considerable light on who BTK is and why the murders, especially the Oteros, occured in the first place. Somewhere in the reams and reams of evidence and information about this case is something that connects the victims, in my view ALL of them, and BTK. BTK did not just pick people at random. There was something they held or had in common. What that was is the key to the complete answer to this case. Hopefully someday we will know what was behind BTK&#39;s selection of the victims he picked, and the motive he had for killing 8 innocent people.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3643-->
<!--Post: 3649--><!--Time: 1105083223-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3649"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 11:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dpinva <BR> <BR>Could the link between the victims bee that it was one of the PARENTS &#40;fathers or mothers or both? or maybe brothers?&#41; of the victims that BTK in fact knew and had an issue with, and that BTK threfore picked their daughters as his victims? <BR> <BR>skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3649-->
<!--Post: 3653--><!--Time: 1105085674-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3653"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 12:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Skov, for now the answer to any &#34;could&#34; question is automatically &#34;yes&#34; since BTK hasn&#39;t been identified. Therefore, why ask &#34;could&#34; questions when the answer is obvious?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3653-->
<!--Post: 3660--><!--Time: 1105102043-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3660"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 4:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tom, <BR> <BR>Asking what could be is how one eliminates what could not be. It is called creative thinking and is a basic investigative technique by which many crimes OUTSIDE of Wichita get solved. As a famous fictional detective once said, &#34;When one eliminates whatever is impossible, then what ever remains, however improbable, must be the truth&#34;. Short of BTK coming in and sitting in the WPD lobby with a sign around his neck that says &#34;Hi. I am BTK. Please arrest me&#34; this is probably how this case is going to be solved, by someone thinking about some evidence, currently known or unknown, in a new and creative way. That starts with asking &#34;what could the truth of this case be ?&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3660-->
<!--Post: 3669--><!--Time: 1105119345-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3669"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 9:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The less evidence you have to work with, the sooner any analysis sinks into a swamp.  Without facts to eliminate possibilities, everything becomes possible.  Just because something can’t be proven false doesn’t make it true. <BR> <BR>The facts contained in Charlie Otero’s statement are: <BR> <BR>1.   Mr. Otero was afraid <BR>2.	Mr. Otero feared physical violence <BR>3.	Mr. Otero was afraid he might be killed [giving his ring to Charlie ”in case something happens to me”] <BR>4.	Days before the murders, Mr. Otero talked on the phone to someone telling them “what he &#40;Mr. Otero&#41; had been up to in the last few years” <BR>5.	Days before the murders, Mr. Otero refused to let a phone repairman in the house until he verified the presence of a company van. <BR>6.	Days before the murders, there was a power failure in the house. Mr. Otero put the family in a closet until he verified power failures in other homes in the neighborhood. <BR>7.	The day of the murders, Mr. Otero drove three children to school an hour earlier than usual. <BR>8.	Charlie Otero believes his father knew the killer. <BR>9.	Charlie Otero believes his family was targeted because of something his father had done as part of his military service. <BR>10.	Mr. Otero was connected to “Inter-American Air Forces Academy” &#40;<a href="http://www.lackland.af.mil/iaafapub/english/index.htm" target=_top>http://www.lackland.af.mil/iaafapub/english/index. htm</a>&#41; <BR> <BR> <BR>	Inter-American Air Forces Academy operated in Panama from 1943 to 1989 when it relocated to the US.  The name “Inter-American Air Forces Academy” was first used in 1966.  It taught the military and civilians of other Latin-American countries a number of skills including counter terrorism field operations.   <BR>	Also operating in Panama in the 60’s and 70’s was the School of the Americas or SOA.  Goggle them and you learn that SOA had courses on how to torture. <BR>	Panama is not that big, IAAFA and SOA were both staffed and operated by US military.  There is a mass of data indicating that SOA taught classes on how to torture.  Part of the manuals are online <a href="http://www2.gwu.edu/~nsarchiv/NSAEBB/NSAEBB122/index.htm#hre" target=_top>http://www2.gwu.edu/~nsarchiv/NSAEBB/NSAEBB122/ind ex.htm#hre</a> <BR> <BR>	I haven’t had much time to look at this, but Mr. Otero was an instructor for the USA in Panama at a time when USA training in Panama included classes on torture.  SOA graduates formed the “death squads” and more. See <a href="http://www.soawatch.org" target=_top>www.soawatch.org</a>. <BR> <BR>	Maybe the part about this being a professional hit isn’t out in left field afterall. <BR> <BR>	 <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3669-->
<!--Post: 3673--><!--Time: 1105122707-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3673"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Devbost<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Devbost<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 10:31 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><b><i>The facts contained in Charlie Otero’s statement are: {snipped</i></b>} <BR> <BR>Any conclusions drawn from these facts are predicated on two things: Mr. Otero&#39;s actions, and Charlie Otero&#39;s beliefs. It is possible, but not verifiable, that there actually was a threat that Mr. Otero was responding to. It is equally possible to draw the conclusion that Mr. Otero was having a bout of paranoia. <BR> <BR>In order to get closer, we need more data, and hopefully Charlie Otero will be able to provide some. Were there any threatening phone calls made to the house? Was there anything else in Charlie&#39;s conversations with his father that indicated a tangible threat was present? Were there any suspicious people hanging around in the neighborhood? <BR> <BR>Charlie believes that his father knew the killer and/or was targeted because of his father&#39;s military service. I&#39;m sure he has specific reasons for believing both of those things, but I&#39;d like to hear him elaborate why. <BR> <BR>As always with this case, we need more data to work with. Any conclusions that can be drawn from what we currently have are too broad to be of much practical use. <BR> <BR><b><i>Maybe the part about this being a professional hit isn’t out in left field afterall.</i></b> <BR> <BR>Yeah, but going from perpetrating a professional hit to becoming a serial strangler preying on women? If we ever do learn BTK&#39;s identity, I don&#39;t think I&#39;ll be too surprised by whatever pathologies he exhibits, but this sort of leap seems counterintuitive. Not impossible, of course, but it seems unlikely. Again, it feels like a piece is missing.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3673-->
<!--Post: 3692--><!--Time: 1105138731-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3692"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 2:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The memories, allegations and theories of a then 15 year old who lost his parents and two siblings in a brutal home invasion murder that have not been substantiated by anyone else who knew the Otero&#39;s is to be taken with a grain of salt. Charlie Otero&#39;s statements are not necessarliy &#39;facts.&#39; <BR>The Otero&#39;s or one of them may have known or once met their killer but this was not &#39;hit.&#39;  <BR>This was a thrill kill by a sexual deviant.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
