<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3771"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 08, 2005 - 10:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><font color="#800000">So are we saying that the Otero murders were originally a hit and then BTK discovered he really got off on strangling people and kept at it?  <BR> <BR>I still am not sure that I am comfortable with the idea of a &#34;hit&#34;, which implies some sort of official sanction. I still think that a more likely scenario is that Mr. Otero knew about or witnessed something that BTK had done that BTK wanted to keep quiet &#40;and in the School of the Americas system, that must have been something pretty sick since they taught people  to violate human rights as a normal part of the curriculum&#41; . BTK, being clearly mentally ill, went to silence Mr. Otero, and Mr. Otero had a pretty good idea that he was in danger <i>because</i> of what he knew or saw. It sounds to me like this was a personal score that BTK settled based on something that happened within the context of the military community at the Panama training command. The question becomes that of wondering what Mr. Otero knew or saw, and what BTK had done that he felt he had to silence a whole family to keep his actions form coming to light. This was personal. <BR> <BR>I am pretty sure that the Oteros were<b> not </b>BTK&#39;s first murder, and Mr. Otero perhaps witnessed or knew about an earlier one that BTK had committed against orders or against a fellow member of the Air Force, or something similar. In short, I believe that BTK murdered the Oteros to cover up another murder, and at some point along the line, perhaps even before the Oteros were killed, BTK discovered that he was obsessively interested and satisfied in binding, killing and torturing people for his sick aggrandizement. </font><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3771-->
<!--Post: 3789--><!--Time: 1105232404-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3789"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Affie4u<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Affie4u<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 08, 2005 - 5:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why didn&#39;t the children try to get out? Open a window? think he had them tied up before he put they in the rooms? You think a neighbor might of heard a scream or noise if there yard wasn&#39;t that big &amp; they houses were close together.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
