<!--Post: 4128--><!--Time: 1105715817-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4128"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cricket<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cricket<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 14, 2005 - 7:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Does anyone know what the morning ritual was of the Oteros.  Did the dad take the kids to school every morning and return home, or did he continue on to somewhere else, maybe work. <BR> <BR>From the other murders I think BTK was after the mother.  Kevin Bright said he thought he surprised the BTK by being there but he continued on in a controlled manner.  I think once he got in and the kids where there that he continued on with his plan.  Then the father came home and again he regained control and continued on with his plan. <BR> <BR>We were brought up in a quite town but were still taught not to answer the door even for a utility person unless you have someone on the phone first and check for the van if they say they are from a certain company.  Being in his old profession probably made him even more cautious then my parents. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t think it was a hit, I think he was after Mrs. Otero...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4128-->
<!--Post: 4142--><!--Time: 1105746259-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4142"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Affie4u<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Affie4u<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 14, 2005 - 3:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why  do you think he was after &#34;Mrs.Otero&#34;?  <BR> <BR>Any idea&#39;s? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4142-->
<!--Post: 4156--><!--Time: 1105781912-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4156"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 15, 2005 - 1:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe he was after Mrs. Otero because she resembles most BTK&#39;s future targets - adult women.  <BR> <BR>I&#39;ve never thought it was a hit, it seems that in 1974 the police held this belief, and I don&#39;t think it&#39;s fair to blame them <i>too much</i> for it. True, the semen and the rope should have been a hint but sadistic serial murderers are very rare, some hits have occurred which feature a humiliating aspect &#40;semen&#41; and the rope may have been construed by cops at the time as having been used to avoid the loud report of a firearm, or as a means of torture. Some hits include torture - &#34;sending a message.&#34; Frankly, the car having been driven to Dillon&#39;s should have been the biggest clue that this wasn&#39;t a hit. Then again, it fits in: this was an extraordinarily high-risk crime and there are elements of control and sloppiness. But primarily control. <BR> <BR>I believe BTK targeted Julie &#40;Mrs.&#41; Otero only. The two kids were ill and would have been presumed in school; why would BTK deliberately begin attacking if he knew Mr. Otero would be showing up? I don&#39;t think he would have, he&#39;s demonstrated too much self-control and planning in the other attacks. He lost control of the Bright scene, yes, but that was a situation in which it seems BTK was surprised. Moreover, he&#39;d shot Kevin and did kill Kathryn. BTK thought Kevin deceased and took off only when he thought he really might be caught. So why did he not flee the Otero scene as he did the Brights? Who knows? He may have been too far into the attack itself to stop. I&#39;d bet he blindsided Mr. Otero, displaying BTK&#39;s particular brand of interpersonal cowardice. <BR>  <BR>Just my opinion. I know what the <i>Eagle</i> said - and contradicted - and I know what BTK has written about this attack. Don&#39;t believe everything you read, especially don&#39;t believe BTK. I believe BTK thought Mrs. Otero would be alone.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4156-->
<!--Post: 4157--><!--Time: 1105782297-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4157"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 15, 2005 - 1:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree george there is no way he knew the children where home. I also believe he waited for Mr. Otero to leave the house bringing the other kids to school. I think he was surprised when he came back. I have always thought that the little girl was hiding in the basement and that was why she was killed there. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
