<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4219"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 16, 2005 - 10:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If that was meant to be a pun, it wasn&#39;t funny. But I do agree with you. I think he preferred &#34;mother&#34; types but wasn&#39;t pleased with Mrs. Otero, so decided to hurt the younger version. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
