<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6813"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 10:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You are right, most poeple think that they were aquainted. Others think that BTK got the information from TV and newspapers and was being &#34;flip&#39;. Charley, Joseph&#39;s son, however thinks that they were aquainted. <BR> <BR>Based on what I&#39;ve read, you are looking at the &#39;hot property&#39;. The experts mostly say that the first incident in a string of serial murders will yield the most useful clues. They also say that the first victims are usually aquainted with the murderer. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6813-->
<!--Post: 6815--><!--Time: 1108018224-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6815"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Icyou<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Icyou<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 10:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->yeah, I knew it has been said that they were aquainted, but it struck me how he referred to Mr. Otero as Joe rather than Joseph Sr. Thought maybe that was significant.  Was wondering if anyone had brought up that little tidbit.  Thought maybe that could be proof.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6815-->
<!--Post: 7183--><!--Time: 1108264011-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7183"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Msrusty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Msrusty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 7:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t think he knew the Oteros. Mrs. Otero could have said something like &#39;Joe, do as he says.&#39; Because I am going to assume Mr. Otero tried fighting when he walked into this scene. He also could have known about the rib injury the same way. Mr. Otero could have told him he had a rib injury while in the process of being tied up.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7183-->
<!--Post: 7184--><!--Time: 1108264377-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7184"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Msrusty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Msrusty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 7:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I forgot to ask about this in my last posting, sorry....Is it known for sure if the kids were home sick or were they just going to be taken to school later that morning? Based on Charlie&#39;s interview, he thought they were at school when the older 3 found their parents. So I&#39;m wondering if BTK was expecting to find only Mrs. Otero home or if he knew the morning routine and he meant to get there while the younger ones were home. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7184-->
<!--Post: 7203--><!--Time: 1108273922-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7203"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Icyou<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Icyou<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 9:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think they were in the process of getting ready for school...targets could have been Mrs. Otero AND Josephine.  I think he obviously knew MR.Otero was away.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7203-->
